  m_overrideMarkdownText: "## API Overview\n\nRequests should start with a base URL:
    `https://api.meta.ai/v1`, and end with an endpoint path. Here only the `/chat/completions`
    endpoint is described. The protocol is OpenAI-compatible.\n\n\n### Choosing a
    Model\n\nWhich models a given key can reach varies by key and account tier, so
    a hardcoded model id may fail with `model_not_found`. List what a key can actually
    use:\n\n```bash\nexport MODEL_API_KEY='YOUR_UNIQUE_META_MODEL_API_KEY_GOES_HERE'\n\ncurl
    -X GET https://api.meta.ai/v1/models \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer $MODEL_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n```json\n{\n   
    \"object\": \"list\",\n    \"data\": [\n        { \"id\": \"muse-spark-1.3\",
    \"object\": \"model\", \"created\": 0, \"owned_by\": \"meta\" }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\nPick
    an id from that list and set it on the client (see <a href=\".\\Packages\\com.meta.utilities.metamodelapi/#selecting-a-model\">Selecting
    a Model</a>). The examples in this document use `muse-spark-1.3`; replace it
    with an id your key can reach.\n\n\n### Reasoning and Token Budgets\n\nMuse Spark
    always reasons before it answers, and **reasoning tokens are charged against
    the completion budget**. If `max_completion_tokens` is too small, the model spends
    the whole budget thinking and returns a `null` content with `\"finish_reason\":
    \"length\"`:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"choices\": [\n        {\n            \"finish_reason\":
    \"length\",\n            \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": { \"content\":
    null, \"role\": \"assistant\" }\n        }\n    ],\n    \"usage\": { \"completion_tokens\":
    32, \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 29 } }\n}\n```\n\nBudget
    for the reasoning as well as the answer, and use `reasoning_effort` (`minimal`,
    `low`, `medium`, `high`) to trade quality against latency and cost. `MetaModelRestApi`
    sends `minimal` by default, the lowest effort the service accepts; `none` is
    rejected.\n\n\n### Text Chat Completion\n\nA chat consists of: an (optional)
    system prompt, and a list of (at least one) user messages. The system role is
    used to define how the AI should behave. The user role is used to pass messages
    or similar information to the AI on behalf of the user. An example curl command:\n\n```bash\ncurl
    -X POST https://api.meta.ai/v1/chat/completions \\\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\"
    \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer $MODEL_API_KEY\" \\\n-d '{\n    \"model\": \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n   
    \"messages\": [\n        {\n            \"role\": \"system\",\n            \"content\":
    \"You are a translation assistant. Translate English to Spanish. No quotes.\"\n       
    },\n        {\n            \"role\": \"user\",\n            \"content\": \"Translate:
    Where is the nearest coffee shop?\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"max_completion_tokens\":
    1024,\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"minimal\"\n}'\n```\n\nExample response:\n\n```json\n{\n   
    \"id\": \"chatcmpl-01a0874f-f364-7a42-b703-f8bc5c6d1396\",\n    \"choices\":
    [\n        {\n            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n            \"index\":
    0,\n            \"message\": {\n                \"content\": \"\xBFD\xF3nde est\xE1
    la cafeter\xEDa m\xE1s cercana?\",\n                \"refusal\": null,\n               
    \"role\": \"assistant\"\n            },\n            \"logprobs\": null\n       
    }\n    ],\n    \"created\": 1788976558,\n    \"model\": \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n   
    \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n    \"usage\": {\n        \"completion_tokens\":
    119,\n        \"prompt_tokens\": 34,\n        \"total_tokens\": 153,\n       
    \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 100 }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe
    completion text lives at `choices[0].message.content`.\n\n\n### Image Understanding\n\nAn
    image can be passed, using a URL or a base64 encoded string. Note that `content`
    becomes an array of content parts rather than a plain string, and that **images
    are only processed on `user`-role messages**:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.meta.ai/v1/chat/completions
    \\\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer $MODEL_API_KEY\"
    \\\n-d '{\n    \"model\": \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n    \"messages\": [\n    {\n     
    \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n         
    \"text\": \"You are a helpful assistant that provides concise answers.\"\n       
    }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n       
    {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"What word best describes
    the object in this image? Only respond with the minimal amount of words. Do not
    include any punctuation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"image_url\",\n         
    \"image_url\": {\n            \"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.org/portal/wikipedia.org/assets/img/Wikipedia-logo-v2@2x.png\"\n         
    }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}'\n```\n\nExample response:\n\n```json\n{\n   
    \"id\": \"chatcmpl-01a131e4-997f-7407-bc88-92cdac5cb5ae\",\n    \"choices\":
    [\n        {\n            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n            \"index\":
    0,\n            \"message\": {\n                \"content\": \"globe\",\n               
    \"refusal\": null,\n                \"role\": \"assistant\"\n            },\n           
    \"logprobs\": null\n        }\n    ],\n    \"created\": 1791838399,\n    \"model\":
    \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n    \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n    \"usage\": {\n       
    \"completion_tokens\": 517,\n        \"prompt_tokens\": 230,\n        \"total_tokens\":
    747,\n        \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 505 }\n   
    }\n}\n```\n\nNo `reasoning_effort` is set in this request, so the service default
    applies; most of the completion tokens are reasoning. Setting `\"reasoning_effort\":
    \"minimal\"` reduces them substantially.\n\nSwap the `url` value for `data:image/jpeg;base64,...`
    to send a local image, and append more `image_url` parts for multi-image prompts.\n\nAccepted
    MIME types are `image/jpeg`, `image/jpg`, `image/png`, `image/gif`, `image/webp`,
    and `image/x-icon`. Inline images are capped at 50 MB, with a maximum of 50 images
    per request. Token usage scales with resolution, so downscaling before sending
    meaningfully reduces cost.\n\n\n### JSON Formatting\n\nThe AI can be prompted
    to return JSON objects rather than freeform statements:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST
    https://api.meta.ai/v1/chat/completions \\\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\"
    \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer $MODEL_API_KEY\" \\\n-d '{\n    \"model\": \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n   
    \"messages\": [\n        {\n            \"role\": \"user\",\n            \"content\":
    \"Dissect the following sentence into nouns, verbs, and adjectives. Return a
    json formatted object with keys: \\\"nouns\\\", \\\"verbs\\\", and \\\"adjectives\\\".
    Do not include any extra information, only the json object: \\\"Where is the
    beef?\\\"\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"max_completion_tokens\": 1024\n}'\n```\n\nExample
    response:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"id\": \"chatcmpl-01a131e3-e15e-7492-ba5f-be0ed3283712\",\n   
    \"choices\": [\n        {\n            \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n           
    \"index\": 0,\n            \"message\": {\n                \"content\": \"{\\\"nouns\\\":
    [\\\"beef\\\"], \\\"verbs\\\": [\\\"is\\\"], \\\"adjectives\\\": []}\",\n               
    \"refusal\": null,\n                \"role\": \"assistant\"\n            },\n           
    \"logprobs\": null\n        }\n    ],\n    \"created\": 1791838338,\n    \"model\":
    \"muse-spark-1.3\",\n    \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n    \"usage\": {\n       
    \"completion_tokens\": 784,\n        \"prompt_tokens\": 58,\n        \"total_tokens\":
    842,\n        \"completion_tokens_details\": { \"reasoning_tokens\": 754 }\n   
    }\n}\n```\n\nThe JSON arrives as a string in `choices[0].message.content` and
    still needs to be parsed. For a hard guarantee rather than a prompt-level request,
    pass `\"response_format\": {\"type\": \"json_object\"}`.\n\n"
  m_overrideMarkdownRoot: .\Packages\com.meta.utilities.metamodelapi/
